# [CHANGE: claude-code | 2026-08-27]
# Single front door for the media server. See DECISION 80.
#
# Why a proxy at all: before this, every app was its own bare-HTTP port and you had
# to remember seven of them. Now there is one address to remember, everything is
# encrypted, and the landing page links to the rest.
#
# TWO addresses are served identically, so one bookmark works in both places:
#   100.82.125.26   over Tailscale -- works on mobile data, anywhere
#   192.168.2.61    at home, on the LAN
#
# WHY NOT THE NICE NAME luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net -- READ THIS BEFORE ADDING IT.
# It was in this file and it had to come out. Caddy has built-in Tailscale support and
# treats any *.ts.net name as ON-DEMAND TLS, which quietly overrides the `tls internal`
# below. It then asks tailscaled for a certificate, gets back
#   "500: your Tailscale account does not support getting TLS certs"
# because HTTPS Certificates is switched off for this tailnet, and falls through to
# Let's Encrypt -- for a name that has no public DNS record, so every attempt fails
# with NXDOMAIN. The visible symptom is not an error: the TLS handshake just HANGS for
# 20+ seconds and the browser spins forever, on every port at once.
# To put the name back: turn on HTTPS Certificates at login.tailscale.com/admin/dns,
# confirm `sudo tailscale cert luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net` succeeds, then add the
# name to each site line and replace `tls internal` with `tls { get_certificate tailscale }`
# in the site blocks. Do not add the name back before that check passes.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO: it does not add authentication. Every app behind it was
# tested first and each one demands a login even when the request arrives from
# 127.0.0.1 -- which is what every request looks like once it comes through here.
# That test is the whole point: Radarr/Sonarr/Prowlarr used to be set to
# "DisabledForLocalAddresses", and putting a proxy in front of that setting would
# have silently deleted the login prompt for everybody. They were switched to
# "Enabled" first, on 2026-08-27, and re-tested through this proxy afterwards.
# If you ever add an app here, hit it from 127.0.0.1 with no credentials FIRST.
#
# ONE PORT PER APP, not sub-paths. Sub-paths were tried and abandoned:
# Radarr/Sonarr/Prowlarr have a urlBase setting, but it only rewrites the UI shell --
# their login page stays at /login and their API stays at /api/ no matter what it is
# set to, so three apps under one hostname all fight over /login. Jellyfin, Jellyseerr
# and luminos-space have no base-path setting at all. Jellyfin was additionally left
# untouched on purpose: giving it a base URL would break the Roku's saved server
# address, and the TV working matters more than tidy URLs.

{
	# Nothing here is on the public internet, so there is no public certificate to be
	# had and no ACME challenge that could ever pass. Caddy signs with its own local
	# CA. The phone shows a certificate warning the first time; accept it once.
	# The real fix is the Tailscale HTTPS Certificates toggle described above.
	local_certs
}

(site) {
	tls internal
	header {
		-Server
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "no-referrer"
	}
}

# --- the landing page ---------------------------------------------------------
100.82.125.26, 192.168.2.61 {
	import site
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8100
}

# --- Jellyfin :8443 -----------------------------------------------------------
100.82.125.26:8443, 192.168.2.61:8443 {
	import site
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8096
}

# --- Jellyseerr :8444 ---------------------------------------------------------
100.82.125.26:8444, 192.168.2.61:8444 {
	import site
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5055
}

# --- NZBGet :8445 -------------------------------------------------------------
100.82.125.26:8445, 192.168.2.61:8445 {
	import site
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6789
}

# --- luminos-space :8446 ------------------------------------------------------
# Its page reads the token out of the query string in JavaScript, so the token has
# to be in the URL. Putting it in here means the hub tile is a plain link and the
# token never has to be typed or remembered.
100.82.125.26:8446, 192.168.2.61:8446 {
	import site
	@needtoken {
		path /
		not query token=*
	}
	redir @needtoken /?token=__SPACETOKEN__
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8099
}

# --- Radarr :8447 -------------------------------------------------------------
100.82.125.26:8447, 192.168.2.61:8447 {
	import site
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7878
}

# --- Sonarr :8448 -------------------------------------------------------------
100.82.125.26:8448, 192.168.2.61:8448 {
	import site
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8989
}

# --- Prowlarr :8449 -----------------------------------------------------------
100.82.125.26:8449, 192.168.2.61:8449 {
	import site
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:9696
}
